// =============================================================================
// Network Service v2 - Comprehensive Network Management
// =============================================================================
// Purpose: Complete network management API supporting virtual networks,
// ports, VLANs, VXLAN, QoS, security, firewall, IPAM, and distributed switches.
//
// Communication: Unary RPC for all operations
//
// This is the largest proto file, containing multiple service definitions
// that cover the entire networking stack:
//
// SERVICES:
// - NetworkService: Virtual networks, ports, VLAN management, virtual clouds
// - QoSSecurityService: QoS profiles and security profiles with ACLs
// - PublicIPService: Public IP allocation, port forwarding, firewall profiles
// - DVSService: Distributed virtual switch management
// - IPAMService: IP address pool management and allocation
// - StatisticsService: Network, port, QoS, public IP statistics
// - FlowService: OpenFlow rule debugging
// - ClusterBridgeService: Per-cluster OVS bridge configuration
//
// Key Concepts:
// - Virtual Network: Overlay network (VLAN, VXLAN, GENEVE, BRIDGE, FLAT)
// - Virtual Port: Network attachment point for VMs
// - VLAN Range: Pool of allocatable VLAN IDs
// - Virtual Cloud: VXLAN tenant isolation
// - QoS Profile: Traffic shaping (rate limiting)
// - Security Profile: Port security, MAC/IP spoofing protection, ACLs
// - Port Forwarding: NAT rules for public IP
// - Firewall: Stateful firewall rules
// - IP Pool: DHCP/static IP allocation ranges
// - DVS: Distributed virtual switch spanning multiple hosts
// - Cluster Bridge: OVS bridge per cluster with role (mgmt, vmotion, storage)
// =============================================================================

